-- title:
--   A prime of the j-integral closure through p=fs avoiding the node
-- statement:
--   Let $q \ge 5$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ equipped with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $a \in k$ satisfy $a^{q^2}=a$, $a \ne 0$, $a \ne 1728$, and lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $f$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$, and assume: as a Laurent series $f$ belongs to `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with $j$ and $j_q$ at the complement of the kernel prime of reduction; its image under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`$= k(j,j_1)$ and is nonzero; that image lies in the valuation subring of the first component of `frobNodePair q a` (the place of $k(j,j_1)$ attached to the point $a$); and it is not a unit there. Let $K \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a number field, $x \in$ `coeffSubring A K`$= A \cap K$ with $\mathrm{red}(x)=a$, and $\varpi \in A \cap K$ a generator of the kernel of $A \cap K \to k$, in the sense that $c$ reduces to $0$ iff $\varpi \mid c$. Finally let $p,s$ lie in `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K`, the elements of `fieldOver (1 * q) K` integral over `jRing A K`, with $f \cdot s = p$ as Laurent series. Then there is a prime ideal $\mathfrak n$ of `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K` containing $p$ such that for every $t \in$ `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) (A ∩ K)` whose value under `pointEval` at $(a, a^q)$ via the reduction map is nonzero, and whenever the corresponding substitution `modularEval (1 * q) (coeffSubring A K) t` of $(j, j_q)$ into $t$ lies in `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K`, that element does not lie in $\mathfrak n$.
--
--   This produces the prime of the $j$-integral closure lying under the node $(a, a^q)$ of the special fibre at which the reduction of $f$ vanishes: it contains the numerator $p$ of a presentation $f s = p$ while avoiding all polynomials in $j, j_q$ over $A \cap K$ not vanishing at the node, so that localising at it inverts them. It feeds the height-one refinement [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_heightOne_mem_of_mul_eq_of_not_isUnit_frobNodePair`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_heightOne_mem_of_mul_eq_of_not_isUnit_frobNodePair) and the nonvanishing statement [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ne_zero_of_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ne_zero_of_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_mem_ssJSet).
